&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payment Methods and Expansion Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with payment methods and financial partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy, and delivers new capabilities in new and existing markets to Stripe users.&amp;nbsp; This is not a traditional sales, channel, merchant-partnership, or account-management role. You will build product and infrastructure partnerships with banks, acquirers, payment providers, and other financial institutions that enable Stripe’s products and market launches. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a new member to join our team to develop and execute on high-impact initiatives with both payment method partners and expansion partners in new and existing markets, focussing on EMEA. These partnerships form the basis of Stripe’s product. As part of these efforts, you will be responsible for deal negotiation and execution for our EMEA payment methods and expansion business. This is an exciting opportunity to make a significant impact and contribute to the growth and success of Stripe&#39;s payment method partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will require close coordination with product and engineering teams, as well as cross-functional stakeholders including go to market teams, Marketing, Legal, Finance, Risk, etc., and with external partners’ senior executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities and craft partnership and product strategies for market expansion and payment method partners in existing markets in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute deals, manage partner onboarding and partnership development for new and existing financial partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand our partners’ strategic priorities, challenges, and internal roadmaps; regularly communicate insights and recommendations to Stripe product stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow Stripe’s relationships with partners, identifying&amp;nbsp; partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, and building alignment between Stripe and our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) and metrics to measure the effectiveness of both deal&amp;nbsp; processes and ongoing partner management and&amp;nbsp; distribution initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience related to payments and/or ecommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep EMEA market knowledge, and a thorough understanding of payment method dynamics and business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple stakeholders with varying priorities and drive creative solutions and commitment to a shared goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a product centric environments with significant internal and external dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders internally and externally across a wide variety of functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Worldwide Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team is responsible for developing and managing a global community of partners that helps ambitious businesses with industry-leading payments and financial infrastructure solutions and services. These partnerships provide Stripe with the opportunity to unlock our market opportunity, supporting us in accelerating our users growth across all market segments from Startup to Enterprise companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow existing, mature, strategic systems integrator (SI) partnerships across EMEA. The focus is on deepening established relationships and improving joint commercial outcomes, rather than incubating or building new partnerships.&amp;nbsp;You’ll manage a defined portfolio of large SI organizations, owning each partnership end to end. You’ll engage senior commercial and technical stakeholders, align on shared priorities, and turn joint partner plans into measurable pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a partner relationship and revenue-generating role. You’ll work closely with regional sales teams and partner stakeholders on joint account planning and customer engagements. You’ll also coordinate with partner solution engineering, marketing, and program teams to strengthen partner capabilities and grow their Stripe practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a defined portfolio of existing, mature, strategic SI partnerships end to end, from joint planning and stakeholder alignment through execution and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with senior commercial and technical stakeholders across large partner organizations, including alliance, sales, practice, and delivery leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute joint partner plans with clear commercial priorities, owners, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe’s enterprise sales teams and partner account teams on account mapping, opportunity identification, and co-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, track progress, and coordinate the teams needed to move joint opportunities forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partner Solution Engineering to deepen partners’ technical capabilities, support training and certification, and strengthen their ability to deliver Stripe solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate targeted campaigns, events, and enablement with marketing and program teams to support joint commercial priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular partner business reviews, agree on actions with senior stakeholders, and follow through on delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand established partnerships across accounts, practices, and EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report clearly on partnership performance, pipeline, risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 years+ Experience in partnerships, sales, or business development within a technology or financial services organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing established SI or consulting partnerships, with an understanding of how these organizations sell and deliver services to enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing existing partnerships and progressing commercial opportunities against defined goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own partner relationships end to end, coordinating internal and partner teams to deliver agreed outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging senior commercial and technical stakeholders within large, complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in joint account planning, pipeline development, or enterprise sales engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand customer needs and explain how a joint solution addresses them, working with technical specialists when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple partner initiatives and work through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for partner and customer engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience in payments, financial infrastructure, or enterprise technology transformation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
